From: OdroidLinux SDK
Subject: [PATCH] client: bare_app: the fit view, the whole screen taken down in linear light (BARE_APP_VCMI_FIT)

With BARE_APP_VCMI_FIT=1 the whole screen is in the frame. Its logical
size is max(w, 800) x max(h, 600): 854x600 on the ODROID-GO Ultra
(854x480), squashed vertically only (2:1 across, 2.5:1 down). It is
drawn at twice that (the xbrz2 setting, images scaled up by the nearest
pixel: xbrz's detail would not survive the way down, its time and
memory would) and taken down to the frame.

The way down averages the source area each output pixel covers, a
source pixel belonging whole to the frame pixel its center lies in, so
no thin stroke is skipped; in linear light, as an sRGB average darkens
the light text on the dark interface and thins it out. Rows go in
parallel (TBB): ~7 ms a frame, ~58 frames/s drawn.

Text: TrueType fonts are drawn at the frame's size, hinted to its
pixels, each pixel spread over the screen pixels whose centers lie in
it (CTrueTypeFont::fitTo/renderInPlaceOf), opened with
TTF_OpenFontDPIRW at a vertical dpi of 72*rx/ry for the squashed
screen. H3's bitmap fonts are drawn the same way by a TrueType font
(FontChain), its size fitted to 0.8 of the bitmap text's width (TINY 7,
SMALFONT 9-10, MEDFONT 10 px); alignment comes through IFont::anchor
(set in renderTextCenter/Right). Layout keeps the bitmap metrics.
Noto Serif/Sans Medium are replaced by NotoSerif-CondensedMedium
(github.com/notofonts, OFL) when it is there: the package installs it
into Mods/vcmi/Content/Data.

L1 switches to a 1:1 magnifier (BareAppLink::magnifies) with the bitmap
fonts pixel-exact, redrawing everything on the switch.

